Passes only if every one of these holds on that run (the forex scorecard, as for trend; the benchmark is holding nothing):
(1) Sharpe above zero after spreads and financing, and the profit still positive with 1.5% a year more markup (profit minus 1.5 x the report's cost per 1% of markup);
(2) deflated Sharpe at least 95% against the forex pool;
(3) Sharpe above zero in at least half of the non-overlapping 2-year windows;
(4) the spread could be at least 2x what it was before the profit is gone;
(5) at least 30 trades, max drawdown no worse than -50%, never wiped out.
Only if (1)-(5) all pass: (6) neighbouring thresholds, 50 and 150 basis points (two more runs, two more trials), must both have a Sharpe above zero.

Reported as information, deciding nothing: financing earned against spread paid, and the correlation of its daily returns with the rejected forex trend run's. If all pass, it may go to the forex holdout (2023 onward) once, through its own frozen note. If any fails, the note is rejected (with Luke's say-so). Run once; no setting changes after the result.
